  "pli-tv-bi-vb-ss3:5.2.1": "",
  "pli-tv-bi-vb-ss3:5.2.2": "Sp 2.693 defines <i lang='pi' translate='no'>pakkhasaṅkantā</i> as joining another religion: <i lang='pi' translate='no'>Pakkhasaṅkantā vāti titthāyatanaṁ saṅkantā</i>, “<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Pakkhasaṅkantā vā</i> means one who has joined the ascetics of another religion.” Yet the idea of <i lang='pi' translate='no'>pakkha</i> also refers to groups or factions within the Sangha, for instance, when the Sangha is split into different communities (<i lang='pi' translate='no'>nānāsaṁvāsa</i>) that no longer perform legal procedures together. As such, it is a term for a separate sect of Buddhism. ",
